# Speyer Tour v3.2.0 — Cursor IDE Rules

## When to use
Implement SpeyerTour when the user requests an onboarding tour, product walkthrough, or tutorial overlay.

## Setup
```html
<!-- With SUI (recommended) — SUI tokens must load BEFORE speyer-tour.css -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/adrianspeyer/speyer-ui@3.5.2/dist/sui-tokens.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/adrianspeyer/speyer-ui@3.5.2/dist/sui-components.min.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/adrianspeyer/speyer-tour@3.2.0/dist/speyer-tour.min.css">

<!-- Standalone (zero deps) -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/adrianspeyer/speyer-tour@3.2.0/dist/speyer-tour.min.css">
```

## Pattern
```js
import { SpeyerTour } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/adrianspeyer/speyer-tour@3.2.0/dist/speyer-tour.min.js';
// Or non-module: globalThis.SpeyerTour is assigned on load.

const tour = new SpeyerTour({
  tourId: 'unique-id',
  // Optional: labels for i18n (partial overrides supported)
  // labels: { skip: 'Passer', back: 'Retour', next: 'Suivant', finish: 'Terminer', stepOf: '{current} sur {total}' },
  steps: [
    { target: null,       title: 'Welcome',    content: 'Intro text.' },
    { target: '#element', title: 'Feature',    content: 'Description.', placement: 'right' },
    { target: null,       title: 'All done!',  content: 'Outro text.' },
  ],
  onComplete: ({ tourId }) => console.log('done'),
});
tour.start();
```

## Rules
- target: CSS selector or null (floating step)
- title/content: plain text only (textContent, XSS-safe)
- contentHTML (optional, per step): opt-in HTML body via innerHTML — takes precedence over content. Trusted static markup only (inline bold/links/code). Never interpolate user input. Prefer content unless inline markup is genuinely needed.
- placement: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'left' | 'right' (auto-flips)
- labels: partial overrides supported (only set what you need)
- Lazy steps for SPAs: steps: () => [...] (evaluated at start())
- Per-step hooks: onBeforeShow (async-safe, return false to skip), onAfterShow
- destroy() for SPA route teardown (no localStorage write); close() marks completed
- goToStep(index) for programmatic navigation; SpeyerTour.VERSION for the version string
- SUI CSS must load BEFORE speyer-tour.css
- No hardcoded coordinates — library uses getBoundingClientRect()

## v3.2 reliability and accessibility

Existing API signatures and storage keys remain compatible; use matching JS/CSS versions. Async hook results are ignored after navigation/reset/teardown; rejected onBeforeShow hooks log and skip. Missing, hidden, inert or invalid-selector targets skip in the navigation direction. onTargetMissing is a notification; prepare/reveal targets in onBeforeShow. Storage failures never prevent dismissal. Floating steps isolate the background; targeted steps keep highlighted controls in the keyboard scope. Run one tour at a time. npm test covers source/dist behavior and browser axe checks; manual screen-reader review is still required for conformance.
